Funny thing is that I've been through NetHack source codes several years 
now and I don't know about this at all.

First of all NetHack has several places where engravings are deleted but 
none of them are associated with unlocking any door. Engraving is 
deleted if:

You dig up a grave.
You bury objects (the code says that it doesn't expect any engravings in 
there but does it nevertheless).
You unearth objects.
The engraving is so wiped out that there is nothing left of it.
If a new engraving is made on a location then the old one is deleted 
(for example can happen if a teleported engraving ends up in a location 
that already has an engraving).
If you engrave with wand of polymorph, make invisible or cancellation.
If you try to engrave with a towel and the existing engraving is made in 
dust or blood or by magic marker.
If you engrave and delete the existing engraving (not always possible).
When a grave is made any existing engraving on the same location is deleted.
If a fountain gushes over any engravings in the resulting pools are deleted.
If debuging wizard wishes a (lava)pool then any existing engraving in 
the same location is deleted.
When a landmine detonates any engraving in the same location is deleted.
If a rolling boulder from trap rolls over a landmine it detonates and 
any engraving in the same location is deleted.
If wand or spell of polymorph or cancellation hits an engraving it is 
deleted.

None of these are connected to unlocking any doors.


Outside of the hero there are six diffrent timed functions:

Buried organic matter rot.
Corpses rot.
Corpses revive.
Light sources burn.
Eggs hatch.
Cursed figurines transform.

No timed function to wipe out 'Closed for inventory'-messages and 
unlocking doors.

If you are talking about Slash'em then mark your message so.

